  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe potential for hazardous weather remains low throughout the\nweek and into the weekend as high pressure persists. \nTemperatures are expected to trend around 10 degrees above \naverage, through the probability of record-high temperatures \nremains low.\n\nPrecipitation chances increase late Sunday into Monday as a weak\ndisturbance develops near the Great Plains and tracks eastward.\nForecast rainfall amounts have trended downward over the past 24\nhours, with less than a 30% chance of exceeding 0.50 inches. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nOver the past 24 hours, long-range models have increasingly\nindicated the development of a large-scale low-pressure system\nover the central CONUS late Monday into Tuesday. Depending on\nthe evolution and track of this system, period of heavy\nrainfall could impact portions of the Ohio River Valley by\nmidweek. Current probabilities indicate a 20-30% chance of\nrainfall exceeding 1 inch.",
